cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LangSlice in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "LangSlice: VLM-driven registration of histological brain sections to BrainGlobe atlases"
abstract: >
  LangSlice registers histological brain sections to BrainGlobe atlases.
  A vision-language model estimates atlas-native AP position through tool
  calls, an image-generation model produces an atlas-colored target, and
  itk-elastix recovers a dense B-spline deformation. Results export to
  VisuAlign-compatible JSON for QUINT / ABBA.
type: software
